From 45b1eec99aa530a958e42f0f6c6b153354b45b25 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "yjqi@YjdeMacBook-Pro.localdomain" <yjqi@YjdeMacBook-Pro.localdomain>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 19:33:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] claudetui: a successful interactive turn tells its account's
 allowance

Since the interactive mode replaced -p for Claude subscription turns
(43966a53, e5f66f8a, 10-31), a turn that succeeded told no
rate_limit_event, so NoteClaudeLimits never ran and the Usage page's
5h/7d figures moved only on a manual refresh (/usage). Only a turn that
ended in a <synthetic> API error told one, from its transcript row.

What changed:
- tap.js, when a main-class reply opens, also copies its
  anthropic-ratelimit-unified-* response headers into the {s, open}
  line as "h". It only reads them; the request to Anthropic is sent as
  Claude Code made it.
- tap.go (rateLimitInfo) turns them into the rate_limit_info -p tells
  (Claude Code 2.1.291): status plus unifiedWindows five_hour, seven_day,
  seven_day_overage_included (5h, 7d, 7d_oi), each only when both its
  utilization and reset are numbers, the reset rounded to a second.
- A streamed reply tells it just before its message_start, as -p does,
  so the bridge keeps it before the reply begins. A reply whose message
  was told whole from the transcript, or that never began one, keeps it
  for the turn's end (tap.settle). Only the latest is told: a kept
  reading from an older reply is never told after a later reply's
  (toldOf), whether the older one ended before or after the later one
  began, since NoteClaudeLimits keeps the last it hears.
- transcript.go: a <synthetic> API error settles the tap first, then
  tells its own rate_limit_info, so the error's reading is the newest.
- docs/subsystems/claude-subscription-bridge.md says all of this.
  The gateway is unchanged: it already turns a rate_limit_event into
  NoteClaudeLimits and limitHeaders.

Run at this head (base origin/main 6c201095):
- gofmt -l on the changed Go files: nothing
- go vet ./internal/claudetui/, GOOS=linux go vet -tags nogui, GOOS=windows
  go vet: clean
- go test -count=1 ./internal/claudetui/: ok (62s)
- go test -tags nogui -count=1 -timeout 45m ./internal/gateway/ -run
  'Claude|Tap|TUI': ok (60s)

Broken by hand:
- tap.go, tap.js and transcript.go at 6c201095 with the new tests: all of
  TestTapTellsReplyLimits, TestTapLimitsOfMessageToldWhole,
  TestTapErrorLimitsLast, TestShimTellsTapLimits and
  TestTapKeptLimitsNotAfterNewer (both subtests) red.
- keepLimits without `n > t.toldOf`: TestTapKeptLimitsNotAfterNewer/
  ended_after red (told 0.42 then 0.3). message_start without dropping an
  older kept reading: /ended_before red the same way.

Not tried: a turn on a real claude.ai account, so the headers were not
checked against a captured reply; Windows and WSL; the full go test
./... suite.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
